        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Constructors should not be passed "as" revivers]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45917</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45917"/>
        <updated>2026-09-28T22:41:27.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Some derivative work off <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3208718025" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40230" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40230/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40230">#40230</a>. I found that the JS pages say to pass constructors "as" reviver which doesn't make sense: first the signature is probably incompatible; second the object is probably embedded somewhere in the JSON payload so you only want to call the reviver on that specific property. Either way, you can only call the constructor "within" the reviver.</p>]]></content>
