    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Migrate Third-party APIs guide to use GitHub public API]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45859</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45859"/>
        <updated>2026-09-28T16:47:45.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #26602.">Fix</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1697657759" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/26602" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/26602/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/26602">#26602</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">I decided to stay away from any service that may require sign-up; readers are expected to have a GH account, so this seems to have the least friction.</p>
