<p dir="auto">The Phaser version was revamped in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3280496481" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40581" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/40581/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40581">#40581</a>, which made it infinitely better than the pure JS version in terms of structure and wording. Therefore, I'm aligning the pure JS version so it's almost word-by-word identical wherever it makes sense. For example, I'm adding the features that were missing—animations, buttons, randomization.</p>
<p dir="auto">I also corrected lots of technical inaccuracies in the original implementation. The current implementation is exactly how real game engines would do things.</p>
<p dir="auto">In the process I also corrected some undesirable aspects of the Phaser docs, such as a few articles being too thin, by merging them. Now, the Phaser tutorial have 12 articles while the pure JS tutorial has 11, with the only additional one being "Physics", one that's purely about Phaser-specific mechanics.</p>]]></content>
